  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760032,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 19 Nineteen: A Commodore 64 Chronicle of Conscription\n\nStep back to 1965 and experience the brutal reality of the Vietnam War in *19 Nineteen*, a visceral simulation for the Commodore 64.  You are a young American draftee, ripped from the comforts of civilian life and plunged into the unforgiving world of basic training.  The game masterfully contrasts your former existence with the jarring demands of military preparation, forcing you to confront the psychological and physical toll of becoming a soldier.\n\n*19 Nineteen* isn't just about shooting; it's about survival.  Navigate grueling exercises that test your coordination, stamina, and, crucially, your morale.  Fail to keep up, and face the consequences.  The game realistically portrays the transformation from a carefree civilian to a hardened soldier, laying the groundwork for the larger, more dramatic events of the Vietnam War that lie ahead.  Prepare for a challenging and immersive experience that will test your limits and offer a stark glimpse into a pivotal moment in history.  Can you endure the boot camp and emerge as a soldier?"
    },
